          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
            %em tensor product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B
            is a new commutative monoid such that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+homomorphism"} monoid homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B \to C
            is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
            out of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            Another way to think of it is that commutative monoid maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B \to C
            are in natural bijection with commutative monoid maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to [B, C]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B, C]
            is the set of commutative monoid maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to C
            provided with the pointwise-defined commutative monoid structure.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CMon"} CMon
              be the collection of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multimorphisms"} multimorphisms
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+maps"} multilinear maps
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1, \cdots, A_n \to B
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \mapsto A \otimes B
              in this multicategory is the
              = succeed "." do
                %strong tensor product of commutative monoids
          %p Equivalently this means explicitly:
          #ExplicitTensorProduct.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
              two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoids"} commutative monoids
              %strong tensor product of commutative monoids
              is the commutative monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+commutative+monoid"} free commutative monoid
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
              of their underlying sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times B
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relations
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1,b)+(a_2,b)\sim (a_1+a_2,b)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi b
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b_1)+(a,b_2)\sim (a,b_1+b_2)
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,b)\sim 0
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∼
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,0)\sim 0
            %p
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, a_1, a_2 \in A
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi b
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b, b_1, b_2 \in B
          #TheCanonicalMap.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By definition of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free construction
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              there is a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              of the underlying sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p_{A,B}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    U(A) \times U(B)
                    \\overset{}{\longrightarrow}
                    U(A \otimes B)
            %p
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon CMon \to Set
              is the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            %p
              On elements this sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b)
              to the equivalence class that it represents under the above equivalence relations.
          %p
            The following relates the tensor product to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+functions"} bilinear functions
          .num_defn
            %h6#definitionproposition Definition/Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              of underlying sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \times B \to C
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+function"} bilinear function
              precisely if it factors by the morphism of
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheCanonicalMap"}
              through a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+homomorphism"} monoid homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi : A \otimes B \to C
              out of the tensor product:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f : A \times B \stackrel{\otimes}{\to}
                    A \otimes B
                    \\stackrel{\phi}{\to}
                    C
                    \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#symmetric_monoidal_closed_category_structure Symmetric monoidal closed category structure
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Equipped with the tensor product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊗
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExplicitTensorProduct"}
              and the exchange map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}: A\otimes B \to B \otimes A
              generated by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo ,
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}(a, b) = (b, a)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CMon"} CMon
              becomes a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+object"} unit object
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (CMon, \otimes)
              is the additive monoid of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              To see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              is the unit object, consider for any commutative monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              the map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes \mathbb{N} \to A
            %p
              which sends for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mi a
                          %mo +
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %mi a
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a, n) \mapsto n \cdot a \coloneqq \underbrace{a + a + \cdots + a}_{n\;summands}
                    \\,.
            %p Due to the quotient relation defining the tensor product, the element on the left is also equal to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo +
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi summands
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a, n) = (a, \underbrace{1 + 1 \cdots + 1}_{n\; summands})
                    \=
                    \\underbrace{ (a,1) + (a,1) + \cdots + (a,1) }_{n\; summands}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes \mathbb{N} \to A
              is in fact an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              Showing that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}
              is natural in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B
              is trivial, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is a braiding.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi σ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma^2
              is identity, so it gives CMon a symmetric monoidal structure.
          %p
            Notice the symmetry or braiding provides a natural isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ≅
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes - \cong - \otimes A
          %p
            The symmetric monoidal structure is naturally seen as adjoint to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+closed+category"} closed
            structure, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B, C]
            of commutative monoids, whose underlying set consists of commutative monoid maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: B \to C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %msub
                    %mn 0
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mn 0
                    %mi C
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f + g)(b) \coloneqq f(b) + g(b), \qquad 0_{[B, C]}(b) \coloneqq 0_C.
          %p
            That
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f+g
            so defined is a homomorphism uses commutativity in the monoid
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo +
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f + g)(b + b') \coloneqq f(b + b') + g(b + b') = f(b) + f(b') + g(b) + g(b') = f(b) + g(b) + f(b') + g(b') = (f + g)(b) + (f + g)(b').
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For every B, there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi B
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \otimes B \dashv [B, -]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CMon(A \otimes B, C) \cong CMon(A, [B, C]),
            %p
              i.e., maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to [B, C]
              are in natural bijection with maps
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B \to C
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: A \to [B, C]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\vee: A \otimes B \to C
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∨
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\vee(a \otimes b) = f(a)(b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\vee
              in the second argument
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              follows from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(a): B \to C
              is a linear map. The linearity in the first argument follows from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is itself linear, and the pointwise-defined structure of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi B
                      %mo ,
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [B, C]
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo +
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\vee((a + a') \otimes b) = f(a + a')(b) = (f(a) + f(a'))(b) \coloneqq f(a)(b) + f(a')(b) = f^\vee(a \otimes b) + f^\vee(a' \otimes b).
            %p
              In the other direction, given
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: A \otimes B \to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∧
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi B
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\wedge: A \to [B, C]
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∧
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\wedge(a)(b) = g(a \otimes b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\wedge
              follows from an argument similar to the one in the paragraph above. The fact that the assignments
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \mapsto f^\vee
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∧
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \mapsto g^\wedge
              are mutually inverse is obvious.
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \otimes A
            and its isomorph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes -
            are thus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            functors, and since left adjoints preserve coproducts, we also have the following result.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The tensor product of commutative monoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity"} distributes
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
              of commutative monoids
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi s
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes \oplus_{s \in S} B_s
                    \\simeq
                    \\oplus_{s \in S} ( A \otimes B_s )
                    \\,.
          %h3#monoids Monoids
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CMon
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (CMon, \otimes)
              is equivalently a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, \cdot)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi CMon
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (CMon, \otimes)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdot : A \otimes A \to A
            %p
              is bilinear means by the above that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1, a_2, b \in A
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a_1 +  a_2) \cdot b = a_1 \cdot b  + a_2 \cdot b
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b \cdot (a_1 +  a_2) = b \cdot a_1 + b \cdot a_2
                    \\,.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \cdot b = 0
                    \\,.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b \cdot 0 = 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+law"} distributivity law
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absorption+law"} absorption law
              of the rig.
          %h2#in_category_theory
            In
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The assignment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \mapsto \mathrm{CMon}(\mathcal{C})
            satisfies base change for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} presentable (∞,1)-categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C} \otimes \mathrm{CMon}(\mathcal{S}) \simeq \mathrm{CMon}(\mathcal{S}).
          %p
            In particular,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CMon}(S)
            is a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mode"} mode
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            a presentably symmetric monoidal(∞,1)-category,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{CMon}(\mathcal{C})
            possesses a unique symmetric monoidal structure subject to the condition that the free functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} CMon
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{C} \rightarrow \mathrm{CMon}(\mathcal{C})
          %p
            is symmetric monoidal. This is due to
            %a{:href => "#Gepner13"} Gepner-Groth-Nikolaus
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+chain+complexes"} tensor product of chain complexes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+modules"} tensor product of modules
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+algebras+over+a+commutative+monad"} tensor product of algebras over a commutative monad
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Gepner13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gepner"}> David Gepner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Moritz+Groth"} Moritz Groth
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %em Universality of multiplicative infinite loop space machines
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.4550"} arXiv:1305.4550
